[Example Rules]
Rule 10 (valid 2D transposed convolution)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ v_3 ≥ 1 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 2) − 1) + shape(v_2, 2) − 2 × v_4 > 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 3) − 1) + shape(v_2, 3) − 2 × v_4 > 0

Rule 6 (last dimension of a tensor matches first dimension of the other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, 0)

Rule 16 (shape alignment for matrix multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, 0))

